    {
      "id": "claim_df2772d6a04a471db8c4535b8a6b955c",
      "statement": "CheerpJ runs in a dedicated Worker (sandbox-worker.js) rather than on the iframe's main thread because a tight infinite loop in learner Java (e.g. while(true){}) would wedge the very thread that must notice the timeout; the Worker lets sandbox.js's timer reliably fire and worker.terminate() hard-kill the runaway code from outside regardless of what it is doing, with the parent's iframe-removal timer as a backstop.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#L104-L121",
