    {
      "id": "claim_d5fae36a3dc444c4b2023ed6c1f4d4c7",
      "statement": "On timeout or Stop the sandbox calls worker.terminate() (a hard kill with no cooperative cancellation inside the JVM-in-WASM), the pending run resolves {status:'timeout'} or {status:'stopped'}, and the main-thread runner tears down and removes the iframe regardless as both a clean-session reset and a backstop kill; memory is not portably capped in-browser, so timeout + Worker termination + iframe teardown is the memory/loop backstop.",
      "evidence": [
